@* Rules text follows the deepseek engine exactly (MoveValidator / CaptureResolver /
   GameController CheckWinCondition) — including the house rule that the Tiger jumps
   horizontally only, and that draws are by threefold repetition only (no 100-ply rule). *@

<div class="modal-backdrop" @onclick="Close">
    <div class="modal-panel" @onclick:stopPropagation="true" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="How to play">
        <div class="modal-header">
            <h2>How to play</h2>
            <button class="btn" @onclick="Close" aria-label="Close">✕</button>
        </div>
        <div class="modal-body">
            <h3>Goal</h3>
            <p>
                Move any piece into the opponent's <strong>den</strong> (🏠), or capture all eight
                enemy pieces. Having <strong>no legal move</strong> loses the game; three
                identical positions (threefold repetition) is a <strong>draw</strong>.
            </p>

            <h3>Moving</h3>
            <p>
                Click one of your pieces (gold outline) to select it. Legal moves appear as
                green dots; enemies you may capture get a red ring. Click a highlighted square
                to move. <strong>Undo</strong> takes back the last move (and the AI's reply);
                <strong>Flip board</strong> rotates the view 180° without changing the game.
            </p>

            <h3>Ranks</h3>
            <p>
                Rat 1 &lt; Cat 2 &lt; Dog 3 &lt; Wolf 4 &lt; Leopard 5 &lt; Tiger 6 &lt; Lion 7 &lt; Elephant 8.
                A piece captures equal or lower ranks (apart from the Rat and trap exceptions
                below). The <strong>Rat</strong> may capture the <strong>Elephant</strong>
                only while standing on land — a Rat in the river cannot. The Elephant can
                never capture a Rat.
            </p>

            <h3>Rivers</h3>
            <p>
                Only the <strong>Rat</strong> can swim in the river, and only Rats can capture
                each other there. The <strong>Lion</strong> can jump the river horizontally
                (across the 2-wide span) and vertically (across the 3-tall span); the
                <strong>Tiger</strong> can jump <em>horizontally only</em>. A Rat on any water
                square along the jump path blocks the jump.
            </p>

            <h3>Traps and dens</h3>
            <p>
                A piece standing on an <strong>enemy trap</strong> (⚠) has its rank zeroed —
                almost any piece can capture it (a ! badge marks trapped pieces). Two
                exceptions: the Elephant can never capture a Rat, and a Rat in the river
                cannot capture an Elephant on land. You may never enter your
                <strong>own den</strong>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired]
    public EventCallback Close { get; set; }
}
